    },
    {
      "id": "sd1863xgZrOoSy7gZ4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3502.5,
      "y": 110,
      "width": 1368.8,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 623598542,
      "version": 40,
      "versionNonce": 845890822,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794409137707,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How would the API and orchestrator scale (horizontally or vertically), and how is load spread evenly across instances?",
      "originalText": "How would the API and orchestrator scale (horizontally or vertically), and how is load spread evenly across instances?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b8A"
    },
    {
      "id": "sd1864N9FzqVCoP2M3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3502.5,
      "y": 141,
      "width": 2023.04,
      "height": 80,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2133504526,
      "version": 40,
      "versionNonce": 1133929205,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794409137707,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Look for: Horizontally: services are stateless, with state kept in DynamoDB / Redis. Names where load is spread: API Gateway behind the api.stampduty / api.chatstampduty domains (managed, already load-balanced); an SQS\nqueue in front of the orchestrator, where each free worker pulls the next turn (absorbs Budget-day spikes, gives back-pressure, FIFO groups keep each conversation in order); an internal ALB across the retrieval tasks\n(round robin, least outstanding requests, weighted). A classic load balancer in front of Servers 1..N is an acceptable first answer. Scale workers on queue depth / age of oldest message. Spots that the real bottleneck\nis LLM quota and latency, not compute: provisioned throughput, cross-region inference.",
      "originalText": "Look for: Horizontally: services are stateless, with state kept in DynamoDB / Redis. Names where load is spread: API Gateway behind the api.stampduty / api.chatstampduty domains (managed, already load-balanced); an SQS\nqueue in front of the orchestrator, where each free worker pulls the next turn (absorbs Budget-day spikes, gives back-pressure, FIFO groups keep each conversation in order); an internal ALB across the retrieval tasks\n(round robin, least outstanding requests, weighted). A classic load balancer in front of Servers 1..N is an acceptable first answer. Scale workers on queue depth / age of oldest message. Spots that the real bottleneck\nis LLM quota and latency, not compute: provisioned throughput, cross-region inference.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b8B"
    },
